# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SEND THE WINDOW AWAY, STAY HERE — ctrl + alt
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Same layout again, without `follow`. Free of macOS: the only arrow-key
# system shortcuts are Mission Control's ctrl+fn+left/right, and you disabled
# those.
#
# KNOWN SIDE EFFECT, and it is the reason ctrl+alt was avoided everywhere
# else. Karabiner turns left-ctrl + left-option pressed within 60ms of each
# other into button1 + ctrl/alt, which is yabai's buttonless drag. So:
#
#   * These bindings MATCH either way. Karabiner keeps ctrl+alt asserted on
#     everything it emits, so the arrow still arrives as ctrl+alt+arrow
#     whether or not the chord fired.
#   * But when the chord DOES fire, a mouse button is held down for as long
#     as you hold the keys. `mouse_replay_click off` means no stray click is
#     ever delivered, so with hands on the keyboard nothing happens — but
#     move the mouse mid-hold and you will drag the window under the pointer.
#
# Two ways to avoid it if it bites: press ctrl and option more than 60ms
# apart (the chord needs them simultaneous), or raise
# basic.simultaneous_threshold_milliseconds' opposite — lower it further.
ctrl + alt - left  : /Users/roelvangils/.config/yabai/move-window-to-space.sh prev
ctrl + alt - right : /Users/roelvangils/.config/yabai/move-window-to-space.sh next

ctrl + alt - 0x12  : /Users/roelvangils/.config/yabai/move-window-to-space.sh 1   # &
